  ▲ Missing format arguments
   ╭─[test.lis:5:3]
 4 │ fn main() {
 5 │   fmt.Printf("[%*d]\n", 4)
   ·   ────────────┬───────────
   ·               ╰── 2 operands, 1 argument
 6 │ }
   ╰────
  help: `fmt.Printf` has 2 operands but 1 argument, so `%d` prints as `%!d(MISSING)`. Add the missing argument, remove the verb, or write `%%` for a literal percent sign · code: [lint.printf_verb_mismatch]
